{
  "part": {
    "id": "places",
    "title": "Places & movement",
    "emoji": "📍",
    "description": "The six local cases (in, out of, into, on, off, onto), which places take which, verbs of movement and postpositions."
  },
  "topics": [
    {
      "id": "local-cases",
      "title": "The six local cases — overview",
      "fi": "Paikallissijat",
      "emoji": "🧭",
      "summary": "Where? Where from? Where to? — answered with six endings: -ssa, -sta, -Vn (inside) and -lla, -lta, -lle (on / at).",
      "requires": [
        "question-words",
        "kpt-nouns"
      ],
      "sections": [
        {
          "heading": "The big table",
          "table": {
            "headers": [
              "",
              "Missä? (where)",
              "Mistä? (where from)",
              "Mihin? (where to)"
            ],
            "rows": [
              [
                "Inner cases — in, inside",
                "inessive -ssa/-ssä: talossa",
                "elative -sta/-stä: talosta",
                "illative -Vn/-hVn/-seen: taloon"
              ],
              [
                "Outer cases — on, at, open places",
                "adessive -lla/-llä: torilla",
                "ablative -lta/-ltä: torilta",
                "allative -lle: torille"
              ]
            ]
          },
          "body": "Think of it as a 2 × 3 grid: **inside vs. on/at** × **being there vs. coming from vs. going to**."
        },
        {
          "heading": "Memory hooks",
          "bullets": [
            "**-ss-** = in (inside): -ssa *in*, -sta *out of*.",
            "**-ll-** = on / at: -lla *on/at*, -lta *off/from*, -lle *onto/to*.",
            "**-a/-ä** endings = static (in, at)… **-ta/-tä** endings = movement away (from)… **-n, -lle** = movement towards (to).",
            "The question words follow the same pattern: miSSÄ, miSTÄ, miHIN."
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "One word through all six",
          "table": {
            "headers": [
              "Case",
              "kauppa (shop)",
              "tori (market square)",
              "Helsinki",
              "koulu"
            ],
            "rows": [
              [
                "Missä? -ssa",
                "kaupassa",
                "",
                "Helsingissä",
                "koulussa"
              ],
              [
                "Mistä? -sta",
                "kaupasta",
                "",
                "Helsingistä",
                "koulusta"
              ],
              [
                "Mihin? -Vn",
                "kauppaan",
                "",
                "Helsinkiin",
                "kouluun"
              ],
              [
                "Missä? -lla",
                "",
                "torilla",
                "",
                ""
              ],
              [
                "Mistä? -lta",
                "",
                "torilta",
                "",
                ""
              ],
              [
                "Mihin? -lle",
                "",
                "torille",
                "",
                ""
              ]
            ]
          },
          "note": "Watch K-P-T: the endings -ssa, -sta, -lla, -lta, -lle close the syllable (weak: kaupassa, Helsingissä), but the illative keeps the strong grade (kauppaan, Helsinkiin). See [[kpt-nouns|K-P-T in nouns]]."
        },
        {
          "heading": "Other uses of the 'outer' cases",
          "bullets": [
            "**Having**: *Minulla on* — I have (adessive). See [[have-adessive|Minulla on]].",
            "**Transport / instrument**: *bussilla, junalla, autolla, pyörällä, lentokoneella* — by bus, train… (adessive).",
            "**Time**: *aamulla, illalla, yöllä, talvella, kesällä* — in the morning, in winter (adessive).",
            "**Giving to someone**: *Annan kirjan äidille.* — I give the book to mother (allative).",
            "**Feelings**: *Minulla on kylmä.* — I'm cold. *Se tuntuu hyvältä.* — It feels good (ablative)."
          ]
        }
      ],
      "related": [
        "inner-local-cases",
        "outer-local-cases",
