              ],
              [
                "ravintolassa / kahvilassa",
                "rannalla — on the beach"
              ],
              [
                "sairaalassa — in hospital",
                "lentokentällä — at the airport"
              ],
              [
                "hotellissa, museossa, kirkossa",
                "kentällä — on the field / pitch"
              ],
              [
                "elokuvateatterissa / leffassa",
                "laiturilla — on the jetty"
              ],
              [
                "uimahallissa — at the swimming pool",
                "mökillä — at the cottage"
              ],
              [
                "toimistossa — at the office",
                "maalla — in the countryside"
              ],
              [
                "kotona — at home (special)",
                "kioskilla — at the kiosk"
              ]
            ]
          },
          "note": "Some places are idiomatic and just need learning: *postissa* (at the post office), *lääkärissä* (at the doctor's), *kampaajalla* (at the hairdresser's), *apteekissa* (at the pharmacy)."
        },
        {
          "heading": "Countries and towns",
          "bullets": [
            "**Countries and foreign cities**: almost always **-ssa**: Suomessa, Englannissa, Ruotsissa, Lontoossa, Pariisissa, Tukholmassa.",
            "Exceptions with **-lla**: **Venäjällä** (Russia), and many islands: **Ahvenanmaalla** (Åland), **Kyproksella**, **Kanariansaarilla**, **Islannissa** is -ssa though.",
            "**Finnish towns**: most take -ssa (Helsingissä, Turussa, Oulussa, Espoossa, Jyväskylässä, Lahdessa, Kuopiossa), but quite a few take **-lla**: **Tampereella, Rovaniemellä, Vantaalla, Imatralla, Seinäjoella**.",
            "Rule of thumb: names ending in a landscape word like **-niemi, -joki, -vaara, -mäki** often take **-lla** (Rovaniemellä, Seinäjoella) — but always check, because many don't."
