    {
      "id": "postpositions",
      "title": "Postpositions: on, under, next to…",
      "fi": "Postpositiot",
      "emoji": "📦",
      "summary": "Words like päällä (on), alla (under), vieressä (next to) come after a noun in the genitive: pöydän alla — under the table.",
      "requires": [
        "genitive",
        "local-cases"
      ],
      "sections": [
        {
          "heading": "Genitive + postposition",
          "body": "Finnish puts these words **after** the noun (post-position), and the noun is in the **genitive** (-n).",
          "examples": [
            {
              "fi": "Kissa on pöydän alla.",
              "en": "The cat is under the table."
            },
            {
              "fi": "Kauppa on pankin vieressä.",
              "en": "The shop is next to the bank."
            },
            {
              "fi": "Auto on talon edessä.",
              "en": "The car is in front of the house."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Missä? — Mistä? — Mihin? forms",
          "body": "Most postpositions have three forms, just like the local cases: **-lla/-llä (where), -lta/-ltä (from), -lle (to)** — or -ssa/-sta/-en.",
